WEBVTT

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.490
<i>I came back here.</i>

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.660
<i>I'm going to play with Nodoka again!</i>

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.090
Yes!

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.590
Just you wait, Nodoka!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.240
That's west.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.340
Nagano's the opposite way.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.690
It's just the feeling, you know?!

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:13.520
<b>Episode 2
Beginning</b>

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.610
Hey!

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.510
Sorry, I'm late.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:17.790
Let's go!

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.870
Except, I've got no clue 
where we're going, either.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.050
You don't know either?

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.470
You said we've got a fourth player...

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.550
Oh, does Achiga have 
some sort of rule like,

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.820
"you have to run an 
interest group for so long

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.170
before you can become a club"?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.050
We're totally fine,

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.140
but finding an advisor
 might be a problem.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.840
Hello! I'm back!

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.720
This is your house, Kuro!

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.440
That's right!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.810
Sorry I'm bringing you from the back.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:50.190
Come on in!

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.800
Thanks!

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.110
Sis, I'm back.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.450
Welcome back.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.890
You're using a kotatsu?

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.720
It's summer!

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.580
Hey Yuu-nee, it's been a while!

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.590
You brought over Ako-chan and a friend?

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.630
Couldn't you have knocked first?

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.870
I feel like I've met her before.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.200
This is Kuro's older sister, Yuu-nee.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.260
She's two years older than us 
and she goes to Achiga, too!

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.390
Your rode the same elementary
 school bus for four years.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:30.980
Really?

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.520
Hello. It's nice to have you.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.300
The rare times my sister goes outside

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.580
she wears glasses, 
a mask, and a scarf.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:42.040
That's probably why you 
don't recognize her.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.900
You were the upperclassman
with the scarf in the summer!

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.580
You were quite the topic
 when I entered middle school!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.620
Don't point.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.880
She gets cold really easily.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.360
But it's summer! It's not cold!

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.670
Wait, does that mean...

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.960
Quite so!

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.660
My sister is our potential 
fourth player!

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.010
W-what?

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.770
She's two years older than us.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:09.980
Next year she'll be a 3rd year.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.140
That's great!

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.070
So, can you play mahjong?

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.940
She's about my skill level...

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:20.070
What are you guys talking about?

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.150
We're going to bring back 
the Mahjong Club at Achiga!

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.780
Please, will you join?

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:33.600
Shizu, you're rushing it.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.830
Look, she's panicking!

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.920
What do you think, sis?

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.540
I don't know what to do...

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:45.970
I'm... so happy.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.400
You know, I always wanted to join

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:56.410
that children's mahjong club 
you were in, Kuro-chan,

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.810
but, by the time I figured it out,

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:05.070
I was in middle school and I didn't 
feel like I could join...

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.980
I was always so jealous of you.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.280
Well, now you can join!

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.580
Yeah...

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.240
Yeah!

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.210
It's over?

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.220
You know our company's 
in trouble right now,

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.250
so the mahjong team might

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.220
get rationalized away
 during the restructuring.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.310
Huh.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:33.850
What do you mean, "huh"?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.770
You work here too, you know.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:38.110
You should care about
what's going on.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:39.200
Yeah.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:40.560
We're off then.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:41.930
Okay.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:44.310
She really only has 
mahjong on her mind...

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.410
<i>Even when it comes to mahjong,</i>

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.580
<i>I'm still not...</i>

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.480
We still need one more person 
to make a mahjong club.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.850
Doesn't look like there's 
anyone good around.

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:09.840
Wait.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.710
What about Arata-chan? 
You know, Sagimori Arata.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.100
Oh yeah, Arata-chan.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.430
Who's that?

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.850
Um, she's my classmate,

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.120
and while we were in kindergarten,

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.560
she would often come over to our inn

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.610
and play mahjong with my 
father and his friends.

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:31.030
Wow, so a kindergartner was 
playing against adults?

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.320
I don't recall seeing anyone

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.240
like that in the children's mahjong club.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.680
Now that you mention it,

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.710
I don't think she was ever there.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.750
Huh, I thought she was a 
huge fan of Akado-san...

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:46.620
So how come she never 
came to Harue's class?

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.940
I don't know, but anyway, that...

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.260
Sagimori Arata-chan.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.980
Could you talk to her?

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.340
About the mahjong club?

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.140
Yes!

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.890
"Strike while the iron's hot."

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.960
I'll go over to her place tomorrow!

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.150
Welcome.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.410
Hello!

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:21.030
Kuro.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.640
How unusual.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.830
Just here to look?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:28.050
Actually, I came here 
to ask you for a favor.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.890
Those kinds of favors tend to not

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:31.920
have any merit for me...

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:33.510
What?

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:38.230
Well, we're trying to start 
a mahjong club at school.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.070
Mahjong...

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.270
Our goal is to play in the
inter-high tournament.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:44.630
Remember how you used to come over

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.980
to our place all the time to play?

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.660
I haven't played mahjong 
since elementary school.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:55.040
Since a certain someone 
stopped playing mahjong...

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.950
Are you talking about Akado-san?

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.640
Is that why you didn't come 
to the mahjong class either?

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.710
I didn't want to see her 
surrounded by kids.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.270
I wanted to keep watching her

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:06.250
in her dignified and strong phase.

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:07.880
I see.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.790
Is she still doing it? That class?

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.380
Oh, you don't know?

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:16.850
Akado-san is actually playing 
for a corporate team now.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:20.780
In the Japan League?

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:21.570
Since when?

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:22.480
Which team?!

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:26.730
It was something from Fukuoka, 
 'Ever' something...

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:31.060
According to Ako, she became 
a regular this year.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:33.990
Hmm...

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:36.900
Well, this next semester,

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.020
we'll be starting up 
the Achiga Girls'

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:40.760
mahjong club in the club room.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.760
Come by if you feel like it.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:44.560
Sure...

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.170
<b>Gifts</b>

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:57.510
It's sad that nobody 
is here to welcome us,

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.220
when there was such 
a crowd when we left...

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.430
This is enough.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:04.200
Triumphantly returning after 
losing in the semi-finals

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.440
is weird anyway.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.290
Even if there was a party for us,

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:08.960
that'd be tough to stand, too...

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.950
Haru-chan, welcome back!

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:19.490
You were so amazing in the competition!

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:22.120
I will continue to root for you!

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.660
Looks like you've got a mini-fan.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.600
Why don't you give her your autograph?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.210
Oh, I couldn't.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.950
My handwriting is so awful.

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.220
Oh, all right.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.350
What's your name?

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.600
Sagimori Arata...

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.310
Can you wash this for me, Arata?

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:55.500
<i>But Haru-chan never played 
mahjong again, after that.</i>

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.240
Children's Mahjong Class
Do you want to have fun and play mahjong?
Where: Achiga's mahjong club room
When: Every Tuesday and Friday 4PM
Instructor: Akado Harue

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.880
Are you interested?

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.250
No.

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:10.640
<i>I rooted for the cool Haru-chan</i>

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:12.480
<i>who played competitive mahjong.</i>

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:33.270
Akado makes a 
comeback from the 
4th south round in
 the league preliminary

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:33.270
Akado Harue greatly 
contributes to success
 in the playoffs

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:33.270
Akado - The driving force 
behind Evergreen's success

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:38.970
The mahjong inter-high 
tournament, huh?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.860
Good morning!

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:52.170
Now that the semester has started,

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.290
our interest group can officially

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.450
use this room!

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:01.630
And... This is one potential club 
member, my older sister!

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:03.680
Thank you... for having me.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.440
Excuse me.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.730
Arata-chan, you came!

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.450
Well...

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:20.110
For now, only as a name filler.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.100
I'm Sagimori Arata.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.120
Nice to meet you.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.190
Yeah!

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.840
How come you're wearing 
an Adamine uniform?

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:31.780
I still go to Ada Middle School.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:34.000
I'll be coming here for
 high school next year.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:37.050
Uhm, I want to turn on the heater.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.260
It's only September, 
so hang in there, okay?

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:41.760
<i>We finally...</i>

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:44.140
<i>got five people together!</i>

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.220
<i>It's happening!</i>

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:23.010
<b>Cable Car</b>

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:32.640
I'll give you a lift.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.650
Nozomi!

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:41.900
You came back faster than I thought.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:45.490
Well, our company really 
isn't doing well.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.370
But you're still employed there,

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.080
even though the team is gone?

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:51.530
Thank God for that.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:53.800
But it's uncomfortable to be there.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.290
Oh, our school.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:58.800
I kinda want to swing by there.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.860
Okay.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.850
My alma mater...

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.620
I went here for three years

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:19.490
and ran the mahjong class for two.

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.020
We went to the inter-high 
tournament from here.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.020
Yeah...

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:29.610
You know, I like it here!

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.210
Huh?

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:41.060
The sign's...

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:43.460
I took that down when I 
stopped doing the class.

00:13:58.660 --> 00:13:59.940
Guys?

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:02.440
Sensei!

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.070
Akado-san!

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.950
And sis? What are you doing here?

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.870
What are you guys doing here?

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:12.370
And you!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.040
You're Arata, right?

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.460
You're the girl I gave 
my tie to back then.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.550
I recognized you right away!

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:21.130
You've really grown up.

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:24.280
What's this gathering supposed to be?

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:27.340
This is the Achiga Girls'
 Academy Mahjong Club!

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:31.600
The five of us will enter
the inter-high tournament!

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.920
The inter-high...

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:36.940
Are you serious?

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.560
They're really serious.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.010
<i>They're really...</i>

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:48.920
I want to...

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:52.500
Would you take me there, too?

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.530
To the tournament?

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.970
You can't.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.260
You're too old.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:00.250
I meant as a coach, or a 
manager, or anything really.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.030
You've got a teaching certificate,

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.720
so why don't you become their advisor?

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:05.920
A new job!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.840
Yeah, our advisor!

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.470
I can't accept that!

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:13.010
Why are you interested
in the inter-high tournament?!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:16.140
I'd much rather see you as a player!

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:19.040
You finally made a comeback
in the Japan League!

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:24.900
That's true, but...

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.400
You see,

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.950
our team was doing really well this year.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:35.330
I was picked as a regular 
player and we steadily won,

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:39.330
but in the playoffs for the 
top of the Japan League,

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:43.080
I couldn't play my best 
and my team lost.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.470
In the end, the mahjong 
team was disbanded.

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:51.450
In important situations,

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.680
when it's a critical point,

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.180
I can't help but remember...

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:59.810
the inter-high tournament 9 years ago.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:06.290
I left something behind at 
those semi-finals back then.

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:11.570
But if I can personally experience 
that tournament again,

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:16.480
I might be able to get it back.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:21.080
So that's why you want to go 
to the tournament with us?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.750
I want you guys to show me,

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.380
how you battle...

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.090
Well, of course we want to

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.540
make it past the prefecture preliminaries,

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:33.920
so it would be really great if someone

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:36.440
with tournament experience 
would be our advisor.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:45.060
Yeah. Then let's all work together!

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:47.020
Sounds good.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:49.800
Then it's decided!

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:51.400
Yes.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.890
To Nationals!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.670
I'm very sorry,

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:17.180
especially after you took 
the trouble to contact me.

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.630
No, not at all!

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:22.370
Thank you so much.

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:24.310
Yes, thank you.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.400
Was that a new job offer?

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:33.810
Yeah. Mizuhara asked if I 
wanted to join their team.

00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:34.830
What?!

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:37.300
And you just turned them down?

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.120
Yeah.

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:40.200
I decided.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.500
I want to go to the 
Nationals, one more time,

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.370
with those girls.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.120
Now, the Achiga Girls' Academy

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.220
Mahjong Club is officially back!

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.820
Now, I know it's sudden,

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:35.070
but this is about qualifying 
for the nationals.

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:36.880
What about the individual tournament?

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.240
Does anyone want to do it?

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:44.310
The individual tournament doesn't feel
 very "all together" like.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:48.450
I think Nodoka was playing 
on a team in middle school.

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:49.690
I bet she'll be back!

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:54.940
Okay, then I'll enter you 
guys in the team tournament.

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:57.520
The prefecture preliminaries 
are in June.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:59.870
If we don't win at the prefecture 
preliminaries in two months,

00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.610
we won't qualify for the nationals.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:03.950
Normally, it'd be impossible!

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:08.180
Because Bansei High's in our prefecture.

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.620
Normally, it would be impossible.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:12.480
As far as I know, they've only

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:14.840
lost once in the 
preliminaries in 40 years.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.550
It looks like it's going 
to be pretty hard to win.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:21.730
But now, the player who made 
that 'once' happen is here.

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:24.930
I guess that's not "normal."

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.670
So, if we all become able to beat you,

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:30.310
we might be able to beat Bansei.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.220
You do know I was playing 
in the playoffs of

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:34.800
the Japan League until very recently.

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.820
Are you sure?

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:40.360
Fine then!

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.530
I'll play you guys all you 
want for the next two months!

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:47.380
Thank you!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.120
Tsumo!

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:54.000
Tsumo!

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:56.130
Ron!

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:08.180
Tsumo!

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:19.990
I'm so beat.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:22.960
I really can't lift my arm anymore.

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:26.720
That kind of looks like 
Bansei's uniform.

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:28.720
Hatsuse!

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:31.540
Ako?

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:33.940
I haven't seen you in forever.

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:37.260
Why didn't you come to Bansei?

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:39.450
Oh, well...

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:40.960
Ako?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:44.570
This is my friend from my mahjong 
club at Ada Middle School.

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:48.790
That uniform... you went to Achiga?

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:49.970
That's right!

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:54.530
But why, when you were so 
into mahjong back then!

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:56.620
Do they even have a mahjong club over there?

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:59.300
They haven't competed in years!

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:02.740
We actually do.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:05.670
Wait, did you not go to Bansei 
because it's hard to get

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:07.210
a spot as a regular player?

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:09.100
No, no.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.660
I want to go up against my 
old friend in the Nationals.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:12.890
That's all.

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:14.370
The Nationals?

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:18.280
We used to be around the 
same level in middle school,

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:20.100
but not only did I not become a regular,

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:22.680
I didn't even make the bench, 
so I'm just support.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:26.000
There's no way you guys 
can beat Bansei now.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:26.970
Hey...

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:30.100
That was probably true until this year.

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:33.730
But now, Achiga's got a great coach.

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:37.560
Speak of the devil.

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:39.670
Shizu! Ako!

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:41.530
We're going back now!

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:43.900
Thank you!

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:47.280
All right... see you at the table.

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:52.160
Hey, it's Akado Harue.

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:52.590
Just move the stuff in the back.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:56.310
<i>That's Achiga's star player who 
beat Bansei ten years ago!</i>

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.620
Sorry, I'm late.

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:08.600
What's wrong?

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.140
Kobashiri-senpai... well...

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:13.850
You're talking about the girl 
in the jersey and her friend?

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:19.150
I saw it when that girl was 
taking bread from the shelf.

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:20.790
She's got blisters all over.

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:23.650
She must be playing quite a lot.

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:27.820
That was probably true until this year.

00:22:31.130 --> 00:22:33.540
Don't worry.

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:38.170
I stopped getting blisters in my 3rd year of elementary school

00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:43.480
Those noobs are no match for me.

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:19.890
<b>Contact</b>

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:10.260
I feel like people who are good 
at mahjong have this aura.

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:13.890
I know, sometimes I can feel
 that they're strong!

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:14.790
Yeah, that happens sometimes!

00:24:14.790 --> 00:24:16.280
Sparks shoot from their eyes,

00:24:16.280 --> 00:24:18.320
or flowers bloom when they win.

00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:19.260
Huh?

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:26.000
Please tune in again.
